# A1/A1.1/A1_09_verbs_review.letz
# Source: Quizlet "A1 Basics Beginner Luxembourgish Verbs"
#   https://quizlet.com/_h2sudr
# Comma- and slash-separated EN translations split into multiple atomic pairs.
#
# The file shipped as a bare infinitive list with no sentences, so it taught 22
# dictionary forms with nothing to use them on. Sentences and @fill blocks added:
# this is the last lesson before A1.2, and the conjugation it exists to review was
# never actually drilled anywhere.
#
# Two rules the fills drill:
#   - the 2nd/3rd person singular changes the ROOT of an irregular verb
#     (goen -> du gees / hie geet; huelen -> du hëls / hie hëlt), so the distractors
#     are the OTHER persons of the SAME verb
#   - the five modal verbs take a BARE infinitive, clause-final, never `ze`
# Every conjugated form used below was LOD-verified.
#
# Pre-existing defect, deliberately left alone: four LU sides appear twice with
# different glosses (schwätzen to talk/to speak, wunnen to live/to reside, maachen
# to make/to do, mussen must/have to). Each is a separate stat key that learners may
# already have progress on, so re-glossing them would orphan that progress.

@lesson A1.09 "Verbs Review"

# --- Action verbs ---
@word schwätzen = to talk
@word schwätzen = to speak
@word ginn = to give
@word hunn = to have
@word sinn = to be
@word wunnen = to live
@word wunnen = to reside
@word heeschen = to be called
@word bréngen = to bring
@word spillen = to play
@word schaffen = to work
@word maachen = to make
@word maachen = to do
@word goen = to go
@word fueren = to drive
@word huelen = to take

# --- Modal verbs ---
@word mussen = must
@word mussen = have to
@word kënnen = can
@word wëllen = to want
@word sollen = should
@word däerfen = to be allowed to

@sentence
@lu Ech schwätzen e bësse Lëtzebuergesch.
@en I speak a little Luxembourgish.
@distractor-en much
@distractor-en work
@distractor-lu vill
@distractor-lu schaffen

