# --- @fill: the root-changing 2nd/3rd person singular -------------------------
# Distractors are other persons of the SAME verb, so recognising the word is not
# enough — the learner has to match the person.

@fill
@lu Wou [gees] du elo?
@en Where are [you going] now?
@distractor-lu ginn
@distractor-lu geet
@distractor-lu gitt
@distractor-en goes
@distractor-en went
@distractor-en going

@fill
@lu Mäi Brudder [geet] muer an d'Schoul.
@en My brother [goes] to school tomorrow.
@distractor-lu ginn
@distractor-lu gees
@distractor-lu gitt
@distractor-en go
@distractor-en went
@distractor-en going

@fill
@lu [Fiers] du mam Auto op d'Aarbecht?
@en [Do you drive] to work by car?
@distractor-lu fueren
@distractor-lu fiert
@distractor-lu fuert
@distractor-en drives
@distractor-en drove
@distractor-en driving

@fill
