# --- @fill: modal verbs take a bare infinitive, clause-final ------------------
# `ze` is never used with these five, so a ze-infinitive is a real distractor.

@fill
@lu Ech [muss] haut spéit schaffen.
@en I [must] work late today.
@distractor-lu mussen
@distractor-lu musst
@distractor-lu misst
@distractor-en musts
@distractor-en musted
@distractor-en musting

@fill
@lu [Kanns] du méi lues schwätzen, w.e.g.?
@en [Can] you speak more slowly, please?
@distractor-lu kënnen
@distractor-lu kann
@distractor-lu kënnt
@distractor-en Cans
@distractor-en Could
@distractor-en Canning

@fill
@lu Meng Duechter [wëll] Piano spillen.
@en My daughter [wants] to play the piano.
@distractor-lu wëllen
@distractor-lu wëlls
@distractor-lu wëllt
@distractor-en want
@distractor-en wanted
@distractor-en wanting

@fill
@lu Mir [solle] muer um sechs Auer opstoen.
@en We [should] get up at six o'clock tomorrow.
@distractor-lu soll
@distractor-lu solls
@distractor-lu sollt
@distractor-en shoulds
@distractor-en shoulded
@distractor-en shoulding

@fill
@lu An dem Büro [däerf] ee net fëmmen.
@en In the office one [is allowed] not to smoke.
@distractor-lu däerfen
@distractor-lu däerfs
@distractor-lu däerft
@distractor-en allow
@distractor-en allowing
@distractor-en allowed to

@fill
@lu Ech muss haut an d'Stad [goen].
@en I have to [go] into the city today.
@distractor-lu ginn
@distractor-lu gees
@distractor-lu ze goen
@distractor-en goes
@distractor-en going
@distractor-en went

@fill
@lu Ech kann net gutt [kachen].
@en I cannot [cook] well.
@distractor-lu ze kachen
@distractor-lu kacht
@distractor-lu kachs
@distractor-en cooks
@distractor-en cooking
@distractor-en cooked
